              ],
              "content": "Table 6.5: Mixing different materials in water"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_table_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.46,
            0.584,
            0.625
          ],
          "content": "You might have noticed that some materials completely disappear when mixed in water. We say that these materials dissolve in water or, in other words, they are **soluble** in water (Fig. 6.6a). Some materials do not mix with water and do not disappear even after we stir them for a long time. These materials are **insoluble** in water (Fig. 6.6b)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.609,
            0.497,
            0.769,
            0.561
          ],
          "content": "**everything you put in water** disappear?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.625,
            0.746,
            0.686
          ],
          "content": "Water plays an important role in the functioning of our body because it can dissolve a large number of materials."
        },
        {
